# Project Rules for GitHub PR Review MCP

> **Note**: This file is maintained in `.github/cursorrules` and symlinked to `.cursorrules` for Cursor IDE.
> For VS Code, see `.github/vscode-rules.md`.

## Project Context
This is a GitHub PR Review MCP server built with TypeScript, FastMCP, and Octokit.

## Code Standards
- Follow TypeScript best practices (see `.github/instructions/typescript-standards.instructions.md`)
- Use Zod schemas for validation
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow MCP server guidelines (see `.github/instructions/mcp-server-guidelines.instructions.md`)

## Agent Personas
When reviewing code or PRs, use the appropriate agent persona:
- `.github/agents/pr-reviewer.agent.md` - General code review
- `.github/agents/security-auditor.agent.md` - Security-focused review
- `.github/agents/code-analyzer.agent.md` - Automated analysis

## Common Tasks
- Use prompts from `.github/prompts/` or `.cursor/prompts/` directory for task-specific guidance
- Reference collections in `.github/collections/` or `.cursor/collections/` for patterns and tools
- Apply skills from `.github/skills/` or `.cursor/skills/` for specialized capabilities

## File Organization
- Source code in `src/`
- Compiled output in `dist/`
- Documentation in `docs/`
- Agent resources in `.github/` (symlinked to `.cursor/` for IDE access)

## Key Dependencies
- FastMCP for MCP server framework
- Octokit for GitHub API
- Zod for validation
- TypeScript for type safety

